9
00:02:37,700 --> 00:02:38,180
No problem.

10
00:02:38,780 --> 00:02:41,660
I wanted to make sure the ribbons were in the right place, so it worked out.

11
00:02:42,520 --> 00:02:45,540
But I'm really sorry that you didn't get to go to the festival with your dad.

12
00:02:46,280 --> 00:02:47,220
Why are you sorry?

13
00:02:47,320 --> 00:02:48,780
He's the one who canceled on me.

14
00:02:49,160 --> 00:02:51,220
But I'm glad at least you have a soul.

15
00:02:51,880 --> 00:02:52,280
Homework?

16
00:02:52,480 --> 00:02:53,860
Of course I haven't done it.

17
00:02:54,140 --> 00:02:56,440
I still have two whole weeks of summer vacay left.

18
00:02:57,440 --> 00:02:57,800
What?

19
00:02:57,940 --> 00:02:58,980
What are you talking about?

20
00:02:59,020 --> 00:03:00,180
That's plenty of time.

21
00:03:00,920 --> 00:03:01,360
Wait.

22
00:03:01,700 --> 00:03:04,200
We're not going because of homework that's not even due yet!

23
00:03:04,740 --> 00:03:06,680
Yeah, that was a real thing I went through.

24
00:03:07,400 --> 00:03:10,660
Not sure why he wouldn't believe me since I'm the one who actually goes there.

25
00:03:11,080 --> 00:03:14,580
He's been asking me to send pics of my homework as proof that I'm doing it.

26
00:03:14,740 --> 00:03:16,520
That's micromanaging, warden.

27
00:03:16,520 --> 00:03:19,700
This totally sucks.

28
00:03:19,960 --> 00:03:22,220
I haven't gone to a single festival this year.

29
00:03:22,940 --> 00:03:23,600
Almost forgot.

30
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:26,120
Iwatsuki had their fireworks festival yesterday.

31
00:03:26,680 --> 00:03:27,100
What?

32
00:03:27,440 --> 00:03:29,160
And you didn't even think to invite me?

33
00:03:29,280 --> 00:03:30,100
Worst friend ever.

34
00:03:30,920 --> 00:03:33,100
Well, you couldn't go anyway because of your homework.

35
00:03:35,180 --> 00:03:36,200
Okay, fine.

36
00:03:36,600 --> 00:03:39,240
I've been out there busting A on a bunch of jobs I got.

37
00:03:39,680 --> 00:03:42,460
So I guess I just blocked the whole summer homework thing out.

38
00:03:43,140 --> 00:03:44,100
That reminds me.

39
00:03:44,100 --> 00:03:46,260
I've been wanting to ask what it is you do for work.

40
00:03:46,840 --> 00:03:47,620
Oh, you know.

41
00:03:48,040 --> 00:03:48,920
Just stuff.

42
00:03:49,180 --> 00:03:49,380
See?

43
00:03:52,920 --> 00:03:53,360
What?

44
00:03:53,880 --> 00:03:54,320
Seriously?

45
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:57,300
Kizakawa, you're in a magazine!

46
00:03:57,600 --> 00:03:59,580
Are you like a new celebrity I hadn't heard about?

47
00:03:59,960 --> 00:04:00,860
No, I'm a model.

48
00:04:01,300 --> 00:04:02,140
Mostly just catalog.

49
00:04:02,600 --> 00:04:03,600
How did that happen?

50
00:04:03,980 --> 00:04:06,840
I was at the salon and this one editor thought I had a good look or something

51
00:04:06,840 --> 00:04:07,980
and asked if I was interested.

52
00:04:08,380 --> 00:04:09,600
I said, sure, why not?

53
00:04:10,460 --> 00:04:11,100
It's cool.

54
00:04:11,180 --> 00:04:13,940
I've just been doing way more shoots than usual lately.

55
00:04:14,620 --> 00:04:15,060
Oh.

56
00:04:15,060 --> 00:04:17,080
Oh, that almost doesn't look like you.

57
00:04:17,580 --> 00:04:18,900
What an amazing shot.

58
00:04:19,080 --> 00:04:19,420
Right?

59
00:04:19,920 --> 00:04:22,800
It's because I've got an actual makeup artist beating my face.

60
00:04:22,920 --> 00:04:25,220
So why are you doing so many additional shoots lately?

61
00:04:25,500 --> 00:04:26,140
You're exhausted.

62
00:04:26,140 --> 00:04:30,560
Well, DSLRs are top dollar.

63
00:04:30,960 --> 00:04:32,140
Gotta write that check.

64
00:04:33,960 --> 00:04:38,340
Oh, uh, Kitagawa's seriously planning on buying one of those mega expensive cameras?

65
00:04:38,340 --> 00:04:41,060
Ugh, I call break time.

66
00:04:41,580 --> 00:04:43,360
Ooh, do you feel like watching a movie?

67
00:04:44,420 --> 00:04:47,260
You really like watching scary movies, don't you?

68
00:04:47,600 --> 00:04:48,680
Like's a strong word.

69
00:04:48,840 --> 00:04:50,800
More like FOMO since part three's coming out.

70
00:04:50,880 --> 00:04:52,360
I want to know what all the hype's about.

71
00:04:52,960 --> 00:04:54,280
Plus, it's what you do in summer.

72
00:04:54,840 --> 00:04:55,260
Okay.

73
00:04:55,560 --> 00:04:57,880
I don't usually watch horror films, so...

74
00:04:57,880 --> 00:04:59,280
How scary are these exactly?

75
00:04:59,280 --> 00:05:03,320
Well, it's just a movie, so it won't be that scary.

76
00:05:03,600 --> 00:05:04,320
You can do it.

77
00:05:04,380 --> 00:05:05,180
I believe in you.

78
