Ah, that was rough.

130
00:06:22,080 --> 00:06:23,820
If there was math, too, I couldn't handle it.

131
00:06:24,460 --> 00:06:25,320
We have math.

132
00:06:25,880 --> 00:06:27,740
But I already finished mine, though.

133
00:06:28,020 --> 00:06:28,680
Wait, what?

134
00:06:28,900 --> 00:06:30,320
But I don't have my...

135
00:06:30,320 --> 00:06:34,900
I'm seriously gonna die.

136
00:06:34,900 --> 00:06:38,320
I think I left everything at school!

137
00:06:41,060 --> 00:06:43,640
They weren't happy that we showed up out of uniform, huh?

138
00:06:43,900 --> 00:06:45,820
I'm so sorry I made you come with me.

139
00:06:46,280 --> 00:06:48,400
It's fine. It's on my way home anyway.

140
00:06:48,820 --> 00:06:50,240
I'm just glad you found your assignments.

141
00:06:50,680 --> 00:06:55,540
Yeah, but seriously, the school looks hella creepy after watching that movie, doesn't it?

142
00:06:55,780 --> 00:06:56,980
It's so dark and spooky.

143
00:06:57,420 --> 00:06:59,400
Not to mention our footsteps are echoing.

144
00:06:59,760 --> 00:07:03,200
If we got here any later, this would have been a full-blown test of courage.

145
00:07:03,720 --> 00:07:04,480
That's true.

146
00:07:04,900 --> 00:07:07,740
Oh, I need to go get some things to make dinner.

147
00:07:08,480 --> 00:07:11,000
I know. How about you eat with us tonight?

148
00:07:11,560 --> 00:07:14,140
Really? I thought you'd never ask me again.

149
00:07:14,980 --> 00:07:17,900
I'm pretty sure she's only been eating that sad fried rice.

150
00:07:18,860 --> 00:07:20,360
So, what you got on the menu?

151
00:07:20,780 --> 00:07:24,620
I was thinking some cold somen noodles with some shrimp, onion, and mitsuba kakiage.

152
00:07:24,880 --> 00:07:26,280
Oh my god, that sounds amazing!

153
00:07:26,740 --> 00:07:28,400
I can't believe you can make a kakiage.

154
00:07:28,920 --> 00:07:30,680
You've got some mad skills, Chef Gojo.

155
00:07:31,280 --> 00:07:33,460
I can't fry anything to save my life.

156
00:07:33,460 --> 00:07:34,820
That's like expert level.

157
00:07:35,860 --> 00:07:36,260
Huh?

158
00:07:38,540 --> 00:07:38,940
Ooh!

159
00:07:40,360 --> 00:07:44,020
I never took swim class, so I haven't gotten a chance to check out this butte.

160
00:07:44,200 --> 00:07:45,940
It's ginormous up close!

161
00:07:46,120 --> 00:07:49,820
I don't know if it's such a good idea for us to be here when we're not on the swim team.

162
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:51,740
I'm sure regular students are allowed.

163
00:07:51,940 --> 00:07:53,540
I gotta dip my feet in for real!

164
00:07:55,180 --> 00:07:55,620
Testing.

165
00:07:55,620 --> 00:07:58,140
I don't think you should do that!

166
00:07:58,320 --> 00:07:59,500
Just let me try it!

167
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:00,040
KiteZa!

168
00:08:01,200 --> 00:08:01,800
KiteGaw!

169
00:08:01,800 --> 00:08:23,400
Thanks, bro. I seriously thought I was a goner.

170
00:08:23,880 --> 00:08:26,660
Yeah, so did I. Do you really not know how to swim?

171
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:30,060
Not, dude. Can't even float. It just looks so nice and cool.

172
00:08:31,800 --> 00:08:35,400
Wait a minute. Didn't you say you went to the beach with your friends around the beginning of the month?

173
00:08:35,780 --> 00:08:36,800
Did you actually have fun?

174
00:08:37,140 --> 00:08:38,480
You mean because I don't swim?

175
00:08:39,060 --> 00:08:39,500
Yes.

176
00:08:41,200 --> 00:08:42,980
I don't mind missing out on that part.

177
00:08:43,580 --> 00:08:46,900
I basically just go to the beach to eat, hang out, and take pics.

178
00:08:47,260 --> 00:08:48,940
So that's how my socks are rocked.

179
00:08:49,400 --> 00:08:50,820
Oh, I can see that.

180
00:08:51,440 --> 00:08:52,380
It's so nice.

181
00:08:52,380 --> 00:08:56,500
I love sitting on the sand, listening to the crashing waves,

182
00:08:56,700 --> 00:09:00,540
and I love watching the ocean get sparkly when the sun starts to set behind it.

183
00:09:00,540 --> 00:09:02,060
It's really magical, you know?

184
00:09:03,080 --> 00:09:06,340
Even if I can't swim, I always jump at the chance to go.

185
00:09:06,340 --> 00:09:19,820
I'm sure that must sound a little crazy to you, huh?

186
00:09:20,020 --> 00:09:21,180
Like, who does that?

187
00:09:25,980 --> 00:09:27,920
What's funny? What did I say?

188
00:09:28,660 --> 00:09:30,280
Oh, no. I'm sorry.

189
00:09:30,280 --> 00:09:33,520
It's not crazy.

190
00:09:35,680 --> 00:09:36,800
I understand you.

191
00:09:37,280 --> 00:09:38,600
I feel the same way.

192
00:09:39,900 --> 00:09:42,400
Even though I still can't paint Hina dolls very well,

193
00:09:42,760 --> 00:09:44,600
I love them.

194
00:09:44,900 --> 00:09:45,340
It's fun.

195
00:09:46,700 --> 00:09:47,140
Exactly.

196
00:09:47,500 --> 00:09:48,680
That's totally what I mean.

197
00:09:49,180 --> 00:09:51,140
I'm sure we all feel that way about something.

198
00:09:51,660 --> 00:09:52,260
I agree.

199
00:09:52,260 --> 00:09:55,000
But not being able to swim could lead to drowning,

200
00:09:55,200 --> 00:09:56,580
so let's not take it that far.

201
00:09:56,840 --> 00:09:58,760
Yeah, I promise I'll be more careful.

202
00:10:01,420 --> 00:10:02,240
Hey, Gojo?

203
00:10:02,560 --> 00:10:02,880
Yes?

204
00:10:03,780 --> 00:10:04,420
Thank you.

205
00:10:04,860 --> 00:10:06,800
I'm gonna look for festivals that are still happening.

206
00:10:07,100 --> 00:10:08,240
Wanna come if I find one?

207
00:10:08,580 --> 00:10:10,340
But what about homework?

208
00:10:10,780 --> 00:10:11,860
You still have a lot to do.

209
00:10:12,240 --> 00:10:13,720
Oh, yeah, that's right.

210
00:10:14,720 --> 00:10:17,000
Okay, I'll finish the rest super fast.

211
00:10:17,160 --> 00:10:18,500
Just help me with the hard parts.

212
00:10:18,500 --> 00:10:21,340
Sure, you've got it.

213
00:10:21,340 --> 00:10:49,060
I'm so proud of Maureen for finishing all her homework.

214
00:10:49,060 --> 00:10:49,780
Yeah.

215
00:10:50,680 --> 00:10:52,100
Okay, see ya.

216
00:10:52,540 --> 00:10:52,980
Right.

217
00:10:53,340 --> 00:10:55,140
You be careful out there.

218
00:11:00,660 --> 00:11:02,620
Have a great time, Wakana.

219
00:11:19,060 --> 00:11:22,680
There are so many people.

220
00:11:23,340 --> 00:11:24,840
I didn't know it got this crowded.

221
00:11:33,620 --> 00:11:36,680
Man, it's gonna be tough for her to find me in this mess.

222
00:11:37,840 --> 00:11:38,580
Where is she?

223
00:11:38,920 --> 00:11:39,820
I hope she's okay.

224
00:11:39,820 --> 00:11:43,380
There he is!

225
00:11:43,640 --> 00:11:44,900
I finally found you!

226
00:11:47,700 --> 00:11:49,600
I'm so sorry to keep you waiting.

227
00:11:51,380 --> 00:11:54,140
The crowds here are crazy, so I had a hard time getting through.

228
00:11:55,500 --> 00:11:56,800
It's cool.

229
00:11:58,100 --> 00:11:59,640
You're wearing your new clothes!

230
00:11:59,860 --> 00:12:01,780
See, I told you they'd look great on you.

231
00:12:02,060 --> 00:12:02,660
Who's high?

232
00:12:02,980 --> 00:12:03,380
Thanks.

233
00:12:03,640 --> 00:12:05,920
And you decided to wear a yukata?

234
00:12:06,940 --> 00:12:07,380
Yep.

235
00:12:09,140 --> 00:12:12,720
I went all out and had someone do my hair and get me into this thing.

236
00:12:14,720 --> 00:12:15,380
What's wrong?

237
00:12:16,380 --> 00:12:18,540
Oh, I think I know.

238
00:12:19,120 --> 00:12:21,120
You're a back-of-the-neck dude, aren't ya?

239
00:12:23,120 --> 00:12:24,360
Wait, what?

240
00:12:24,360 --> 00:12:28,960
Um, well, uh, I wouldn't say that.

241
00:12:29,700 --> 00:12:31,360
Uh, uh...

242
00:12:31,960 --> 00:12:33,720
No way!

243
00:12:34,320 --> 00:12:35,200
For real?

244
00:12:35,640 --> 00:12:37,960
For really, really, really, really, really, really, really, really?

245
00:12:40,960 --> 00:12:43,460
I couldn't choke on how hyped I am right now!

246
00:12:43,820 --> 00:12:45,500
I'm so glad I wore a yukata!

247
00:12:46,220 --> 00:12:48,500
I'm death-dropping neck bombs out here!

248
00:12:50,500 --> 00:12:53,500
So, any idea what time the fireworks show starts?

249
00:12:54,360 --> 00:12:56,580
Are you excited or angry right now?

250
00:13:00,080 --> 00:13:02,060
Look, they have candy apples there!

251
00:13:05,400 --> 00:13:06,720
I'm going in!

252
00:13:07,120 --> 00:13:08,400
Everything here looks great!

253
00:13:10,680 --> 00:13:12,080
Oh, okonomiyaki!

254
00:13:13,360 --> 00:13:14,080
Thank you!

255
00:13:14,920 --> 00:13:16,240
This looks amazing!

256
00:13:16,640 --> 00:13:17,000
Kitagawa!

257
00:13:17,720 --> 00:13:18,240
Huh?

258
00:13:18,780 --> 00:13:19,020
Huh?

259
00:13:19,660 --> 00:13:21,180
They have yakitori, too!

260
00:13:21,300 --> 00:13:22,020
Nice and hot!

261
00:13:23,040 --> 00:13:23,520
Right.

262
00:13:24,320 --> 00:13:25,360
We're not done yet!

263
00:13:31,360 --> 00:13:37,000
This is a lot of food!

264
00:13:38,640 --> 00:13:40,300
Had to get enough for two people!

265
00:13:40,660 --> 00:13:40,900
Wow!

266
00:13:42,060 --> 00:13:43,840
Let's go slam it down in the plaza!

267
00:13:44,520 --> 00:13:45,740
Thank you for your patience!

268
00:13:45,740 --> 00:13:49,680
We're excited to announce that the fireworks show will start momentarily!

269
00:13:49,960 --> 00:13:50,580
Please enjoy!

270
00:13:50,800 --> 00:13:51,140
Crap!

271
00:13:51,220 --> 00:13:52,280
We better hurry up, Gojo!

272
00:13:52,880 --> 00:13:53,280
Right!

273
00:13:54,880 --> 00:13:58,900
You know, this is actually my first time coming down to the plaza to watch the fireworks!

274
00:13:59,260 --> 00:13:59,660
Seriously?

275
00:13:59,860 --> 00:14:00,340
No way!

276
00:14:01,040 --> 00:14:03,700
